{
  // `tsconfig.json` excludes `src/__tests__` because tests are not compiled into dist/, and
  // `tsconfig.real-tests.json` covers only `scripts/real-tests`. That left the unit tests
  // typechecked by nothing: vitest transpiles without checking, so a test can pass an argument
  // whose type no longer exists and stay green.
  //
  // That is not hypothetical. A hardcoded "stdin-error" death event outlived its union member by a
  // commit; the call still satisfied its assertion by falling through every branch, so the suite
  // reported 18/18 while one iteration asserted about an input no caller could produce. The commit
  // that removed the member is the one whose message argued this directory needed typechecking.
  //
  // Scope: the hyper-v-windows session files only. Turning this on for all of `src/__tests__`
  // surfaces ~740 pre-existing errors (349 here, 391 more dragged in from `scripts/real-tests`),
  // which is its own piece of work and not this feature's to absorb. These are the files this
  // feature owns and keeps editing, and the drift above is exactly the failure they are prone to.
  // Widening the `include` below is the way to pay down the rest.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "rootDir": "./src"
  },
  "include": [
    "src/__tests__/hyper-v-windows-session-pool.test.ts",
    "src/__tests__/hyper-v-windows-session.test.ts",
    "src/__tests__/hyper-v-windows-session-adapter.test.ts",
    "src/__tests__/hyper-v-windows-session-property.test.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": []
}
